% ABSTRACT
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\begin{abstract}
We present the Temporal Symmetry Astrophysics Simulation Engine (TSSE), a
large-scale Hamiltonian simulation framework achieving fully symplectic,
time-reversible evolution for up to $N = 10^9$ interacting bodies under
Newtonian gravity with post-Newtonian relativistic corrections. The engine
implements symmetric partitioned Runge--Kutta composition integrators paired
with an explicit time-reversal involution, guaranteeing Liouville-compliant
phase-space evolution. Empirical validation demonstrates relative energy drift
bounded by $\Delta E / E \le 4.18 \times 10^{-15}$ and effective Lyapunov
divergence below $1.09 \times 10^{-16}$, with bit-exact reversibility on
analytically controlled subsets. These results indicate unprecedented numerical
fidelity and temporal symmetry at astrophysical scale.
\end{abstract}

