\section{Introduction}
Astrophysical $N$-body simulations traditionally suffer from secular energy
drift, non-reversible trajectories, and violations of Liouville's theorem due
to floating-point asymmetries and non-symplectic integration schemes. The
Temporal Symmetry Astrophysics Simulation Engine (TSSE) addresses these
limitations by enforcing exact time symmetry and symplectic structure at
billion-body scale.

