\section{Hamiltonian Framework}
Let $\mathcal{M}$ be a $2n$-dimensional phase space with canonical coordinates
$(q,p)$ and symplectic form $\omega = \sum dq_i \wedge dp_i$. The Hamiltonian
\[
H(q,p) = T(p) + V(q)
\]
governs the continuous flow $\Phi_t$, which satisfies Hamilton's equations and
preserves $\omega$.

