\section{Methods}
\subsection{Integration Scheme}
TSSE employs Yoshida-type symmetric compositions of partitioned Runge--Kutta
substeps, ensuring time symmetry and symplecticity.

\subsection{Time-Reversal Operator}
The involution $\mathcal{T}(q,p,t) = (q,-p,-t)$ is applied at the midpoint of
the forward-backward cycle.

\subsection{Bit-Level Verification}
State buffers $S_0$ and $S_f$ are serialized in IEEE 754 double precision and
compared via XOR reduction:
\[
\Delta_{\text{bits}} = \bigoplus (S_f \oplus S_0).
\]

